32597c7522ff828ba54d33f4","commit_subject":"Official servers prove themselves to the masterserver with one secret: report_ranked_match_api_key is now official_server_secret, from which the server derives (HMAC-SHA256 with distinct contexts) a key id, a heartbeat key and the netcode key for the upcoming secure connections; heartbeats and goodbyes carry a signature (key id, a strictly increasing millisecond timestamp, a MAC over the whole serialized request), and the masterserver lists a server as official only if the signature verifies against a file in official_servers_dir (file name = server id, content = its secret, rescanned every minute) with a clock within 30 s and a timestamp newer than the last, in place of official_hosts resolved over DNS, which made any port on an official host's IP, or any spoofed UDP source, official; unauthenticated heartbeats and goodbyes from an official address are ignored, so nobody else can rename an official server, change its ranked status or take it off the list","ai_tool":"Claude"},{"repo_name":"maksimkurb/keen-pbr","commit_timestamp":"2026-10-10T21:18:32Z","branch":"main","commit_sha":"b23f1adb4fbae72114e7881142e4e8355b66a542","github_link":"https://github.com/maksimkurb/keen-pbr/commit/b23f1adb4fbae72114e7881142e4e8355b66a542","commit_subject":"docs: rewrite user docs for people and drop internal notes","ai_tool":"Claude"},{"repo_name":"TeamHypersomnia/Hypersomnia","commit_timestamp":"2026-10-10T21:18:23Z","branch":"master","commit_sha":"13a7eb8a7870a6a1022db74056b3aea53ecd17be","github_link":"https://github.com/TeamHypersomnia/Hypersomnia/commit/13a7eb8a7870a6a1022db74056b3aea53ecd17be","commit_subject":"augs::hmac_sha256 through OpenSSL (std::nullopt without it, e.g. on the web) and augs::constant_time_equal for comparing MACs","ai_tool":"Claude"},{"repo_name":"fwupd/fwupd","commit_timestamp":"2026-10-10T21:18:22Z","branch":"main","commit_sha":"80c7bf5d26f3435ce8950fffbff5f5a2a33a62df","github_link":"https://github.com/fwupd/fwupd/commit/80c7bf5d26f3435ce8950fffbff5f5a2a33a62df","commit_subject":"vbe: Fix parsing of the storage device number","ai_tool":"Claude"},{"repo_name":"getlantern/radiance","commit_timestamp":"2026-10-10T21:18:02Z","branch":"main","commit_sha":"568e3166a1888d78d92ce48399fe746ab5798103","github_link":"https://github.com/getlantern/radiance/commit/568e3166a1888d78d92ce48399fe746ab5798103","commit_subject":"test: serialize tests that use the fixed bypass port across packages","ai_tool":"Claude"},{"repo_name":"LoveDaisy/Lumice","commit_timestamp":"2026-10-10T21:17:42Z","branch":"main","commit_sha":"6d37da11a03aab3eef379f5d90082abbe7e1fa44","github_link":"https://github.com/LoveDaisy/Lumice/commit/6d37da11a03aab3eef379f5d90082abbe7e1fa44","commit_subject":"docs(test-cost): record first acceptance sample","ai_tool":"Claude"},{"repo_name":"jpettitt/weather-radar-card","commit_timestamp":"2026-10-10T21:17:39Z","branch":"main","commit_sha":"9ad906658ab3dee09a8ef67a5371f18d14421e30","github_link":"https://github.com/jpettitt/weather-radar-card/commit/9ad906658ab3dee09a8ef67a5371f18d14421e30","commit_subject":"fix(tiles): end retry chains with the tile and cap rate-limit retries","ai_tool":"Claude"},{"repo_name":"RustPython/RustPython","commit_timestamp":"2026-10-10T21:17:08Z","branch":"main","commit_sha":"eb6cefd76509b6cd3103ff2e90deca5072e23050","github_link":"https://github.com/RustPython/RustPython/commit/eb6cefd76509b6cd3103ff2e90deca5072e23050","commit_subject":"Mark LRU cache wrappers as method descriptors (#9072)","ai_tool":"Codex"},{"repo_name":"moq-dev/moq","commit_timestamp":"2026-10-10T21:16:53Z","branch":"main","commit_sha":"cabdaf2d347650066bd61152be4fc344b897cd1a","github_link":"https://github.com/moq-dev/moq/commit/cabdaf2d347650066bd61152be4fc344b897cd1a","commit_subject":"quest(m1): delete pool-churn-cursors, done by #5182 (#5255)","ai_tool":"Claude"},{"repo_name":"ClickHouse/ClickHouse","commit_timestamp":"2026-10-10T21:16:04Z","branch":"master","commit_s